<header class="world-hero"><span class="world-kicker">UNDER THE HOOD / PROJECT ZERO</span><h1>The website is part of the portfolio.</h1><p>This is the implementation surface: the same site you are reading, described using technologies and delivery choices that are actually present in the repository.</p></header>
<section class="world-section"><div class="world-section-head"><span>RUNTIME</span><h2>Small stack. Explicit boundaries.</h2></div><div class="hood-grid"><article><span>APPLICATION</span><h3>PHP 8.3</h3><p>Server-rendered pages, route handling, validation and application services.</p></article><article><span>DATA</span><h3>PostgreSQL</h3><p>Structured project, profile, engineering and inquiry data with numbered migrations.</p></article><article><span>DELIVERY</span><h3>Docker + Apache</h3><p>The repository includes a Docker image and Apache configuration for the application runtime.</p></article><article><span>DEPLOYMENT</span><h3>Render configuration</h3><p>The repository contains a Render service definition and a database definition. Runtime availability is not inferred from configuration alone.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="world-section"><div class="world-section-head"><span>DELIVERY DISCIPLINE</span><h2>What the repository already enforces.</h2></div><div class="proof-list"><div><b>01</b><span>Idempotent database migrations</span><p>Migration versions are tracked before changes are applied.</p></div><div><b>02</b><span>Document-root separation</span><p>Server-side templates live outside the public Apache document root.</p></div><div><b>03</b><span>Health endpoint</span><p>The deployment configuration points to a dedicated health endpoint.</p></div><div><b>04</b><span>Validation scripts</span><p>The repository documents PHP syntax checks, smoke tests and diff checks.</p></div></div></section>
